<%# A destructive button that asks first, in place: the button opens a small panel under it with
    what will happen and the real button. A <details>, so it needs no script, and a second click
    on the button is the Cancel. Never a modal — this already lives in one, and the modal frame is
    the dialog itself.

    locals: label (the button), text (what happens), confirm (the real button's label), url,
            method (default :delete), params (optional hidden fields) %>
<details class="sconfirm">
  <summary class="rbutton rbutton--secondary"><%= label %></summary>
  <div class="sconfirm__panel">
    <p><%= text %></p>
    <%= button_to confirm, url, method: local_assigns.fetch(:method, :delete), params: local_assigns.fetch(:params, {}),
                  class: 'rbutton rbutton--secondary rbutton--danger' %>
  </div>
</details>
